 token. Only allowed by the SUPERVISOR role."},"burn(uint256)":{"details":"Burns tokens from the caller.","params":{"amount":"Amount to decrease the supply by."}},"constructor":{"details":"Initializes the contract.","params":{"mintableToken":"The address of the mintable ERC20 token."}},"getRoleAdmin(bytes32)":{"details":"Returns the admin role that controls `role`. See {grantRole} and {revokeRole}. To change a role's admin, use {_setRoleAdmin}."},"getRoleMember(bytes32,uint256)":{"details":"Returns one of the accounts that have `role`. `index` must be a value between 0 and {getRoleMemberCount}, non-inclusive. Role bearers are not sorted in any particular way, and their ordering may change at any point. WARNING: When using {getRoleMember} and {getRoleMemberCount}, make sure you perform all queries on the same block. See the following https://forum.openzeppelin.com/t/iterating-over-elements-on-enumerableset-in-openzeppelin-contracts/2296[forum post] for more information."},"getRoleMemberCount(bytes32)":{"details":"Returns the number of accounts that have `role`. Can be used together with {getRoleMember} to enumerate all bearers of a role."},"grantRole(bytes32,address)":{"details":"Grants `role` to `account`. If `account` had not been already granted `role`, emits a {RoleGranted} event. Requirements: - the caller must have ``role``'s admin role."},"hasRole(bytes32,address)":{"details":"Returns `true` if `account` has been granted `role`."},"mint(address,uint256)":{"details":"Mints new tokens. Only allowed by the MINTER role.","params":{"amount":"Amount to increase the supply by.","to":"Account to receive the new amount."}},"renounceRole(bytes32,address)":{"details":"Revokes `role` from the calling account. Roles are often managed via {grantRole} and {revokeRole}: this function's purpose is to provide a mechanism for accounts to lose their privileges if they are compromised (such as when a trusted device is misplaced). If the calling account had been granted `role`, emits a {RoleRevoked} event. Requirements: - the caller must be `account`."},"revokeRole(bytes32,address)":{"details":"Revokes `role` from `account`. If `account` had been granted `role`, emits a {RoleRevoked} event. Requirements: - the caller must have ``role``'s admin role."}},"title":"The Token Governance contract is used to govern a mintable ERC20 token by restricting its launch-time initial administrative privileges.","version":1},"userdoc":{"kind":"user","methods":{},"version":1}},"settings":{"compilationTarget":{"/Users/yudi/git/token-governance/contracts/TokenGovernance.sol":"TokenGovernance"},"evmVersion":"istanbul","libraries":{},"metadata":{"bytecodeHash":"ipfs"},"optimizer":{"enabled":true,"runs":200},"remappings":[]},"sources":{"/Users/yudi/git/token-governance/contracts/IClaimable.sol":{"keccak256":"0x17620afd14ae6f799589f76369ab27e95110f8ce47cf26979394aba6fd3f07a2","license":"MIT","urls":["bzz-raw://ba8a42b6f6d645d40a90c655a4b2de34cefa609891443d60746969a2c731b113","dweb:/ipfs/QmNdYvF3NcfchDtA8wzDXpt93u9tUMUnBVKjeXnUdhajJ6"]},"/Users/yudi/git/token-governance/contracts/IMintableToken.sol":{"keccak256":"0x143d85ba15d10c0c6229f86d42f2ff603f87517026fc7924dc438fca180640e8","license":"MIT","urls":["bzz-raw://ae886e54a525ca6c17dd008482c637e68b136cec366f78c6483f75b6e2ce3e1c","dweb:/ipfs/QmSN1pBNmtU3RwKp43UmrsR94Ud6XxF5zsCHuHj1D2pHqD"]},"/Users/yudi/git/token-governance/contracts/ITokenGovernance.sol":{"keccak256":"0x557afb8adfc5c47781d178062fa3db30b18718ea5d8446e8077e8f8252f19e1d","license":"MIT","urls":["bzz-raw://e8119d8fcdb47f5397b0386dd0628393fe36d182177e26020199048a3f722400","dweb:/ipfs/QmanqurG1Z65pA63JKyaxS4mpSwpyhroVVe9RZa2WSySNh"]},"/Users/yudi/git/token-governance/contracts/TokenGovernance.sol":{"keccak256":"0xddc8c7066c42502951fa23eaa28c74f56b85b11a62cf596ed963d10db70a7ea1","license":"MIT","urls":["bzz-raw://c154a5aded74aa71261c7623a8df4662653191719489d5a771feb82d3c666adf","dweb:/ipfs/QmVnG6TaeXxUcs4JshqYHDaHJyLewWMzBuwpB5Ht6cvDNV"]},"@openzeppelin/co